  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">2025 - Funding Model Surge Deployments &amp; Capacity Enhancement Africa &amp; MENA Region</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">National Societies surge readiness: This model strengthens NS ability to respond effectively by providing additional support for:
o Increased competencies through access to learning and development, including essential operational trainings, developing and exchange missions, mentoring, and other capacity-enhancement opportunities.
o Ensure NS are Surge ready through an increased compliance with duty of care, safeguarding mechanism for an effective support neighboring National Societies.
Enhanced National Societies capacities through regional deployments: Resources will be directed toward deploying skilled personnel from National Societies within the region, ensuring faster, more effective, and locally led responses that build trust and impact within affected communities. It is expected that regionally deployed response personnel will also contribute to strengthening their receiving NS by applying the experience gained.

Reinforced solidarity mechanism among NS in the region, ensuring stronger connection, experience sharing and trust build that will be translated into a more solid regional
mechanism.

Increased autonomy and reduced dependency for global wider surge mechanisms.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Surge Funding Model Initiative is a strategic mechanism designed to remove financial barriers that prevent capable National Societies (NS) in disaster- and crisis-prone regions from deploying skilled personnel within their own region. This model enables faster, more cost-effective and locally driven responses while enhancing autonomy, strengthening regional networks, and increasing local-to-regional capacity.</narrative>
  </description>
